 ## The elevation scale and the overlay
 
+*Legacy:* for a control not migrated yet. In the design system only what floats has a shadow:
+`shadow-menu` becomes `--tl-shadow-popover`, `shadow-dialog` becomes `--tl-shadow-dialog`, a dragged
+element takes `--tl-shadow-drag`, `overlay` becomes `--tl-surface-scrim`; `shadow-raised` has no
+successor (a surface on the page is told apart by its surface role and border, not by a shadow), and
+the dialog backdrop of the design system does not blur (`surface-blur` is no longer read there).
+
 Drop shadows come in three steps, each a `<text>` token, and a backdrop takes the overlay token:
 
